{{!
    @template theme_nit/navbar_lang_toggle

    The navbar language control on a two-language site: one button that swaps
    straight to the other language, instead of a dropdown offering the single
    alternative. Rendered by theme_nit\output\core_renderer::navbar_language_menu()
    (which falls back to core's dropdown once a third language is installed).

    The label is the language the button switches TO — the site in English shows
    "AR" — because the control performs the switch rather than reporting the
    current state. Two letters say very little read aloud, so the accessible name
    and the tooltip carry the language's full name.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * url - the ?lang=xx URL that switches to the other language
    * label - two-letter code of that language, upper case ("AR" / "EN")
    * title - that language's own full name ("العربية"), for title/aria-label
    * langcode - that language's code ("ar" / "en"), for the hreflang hint

    Example context (json):
    {
        "url": "https://example.com/course/view.php?id=2&lang=ar",
        "label": "AR",
        "title": "العربية (ar)",
        "langcode": "ar"
    }
}}
<div class="langmenu nit-langtoggle-wrap">
    <a href="{{{url}}}" class="btn nit-langtoggle" title="{{title}}" aria-label="{{title}}"
       {{#langcode}}hreflang="{{langcode}}"{{/langcode}} data-nit-lang-toggle>
        <i class="icon fa fa-language fa-fw me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <span class="langbutton">{{label}}</span>
    </a>
</div>
